{
  "dom_id": "step-q214107",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "If ${a}_{n+1}=2-5{a}_{n}$ with ${a}_{1}=-3,$ then ${a}_{2}=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=2-5{a}_{n}\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}=-3.$\n\nWe compute ${a}_{2}$ by substituting $n=1$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n+1} & =2-5{a}_{n} \\\\ {a}_{1+1} & =2-5{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2-5{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2-5(-3) \\\\ {a}_{2} & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${a}_{2}=17.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
